        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Firefox 158 nightly supports streaming fetch() request body]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30794</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30794"/>
        <updated>2026-10-08T11:30:15.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Fx 158 enables support for <code class="notranslate">ReadableStream</code> request bodies in <code class="notranslate">fetch()</code> requests, in Nightly only for now. See <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1594633" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1594633</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The bug is a bit complex to follow, but from what I can see, both the <code class="notranslate">accepts_readablestream</code> and <code class="notranslate">duplex</code> data points need setting to preview. Both are gated by the <code class="notranslate">dom.fetch.streaming_upload</code> pref, and <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/web-apis/fetch-streaming-requests" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/web-apis/fetch-streaming-requests</a> points out that <code class="notranslate">duplex: "half"</code> needs to be set to allow streams to be used in a request.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5617201808" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45887" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45887/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45887">mdn/content#45887</a></p>

]]></content>
